WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.787
The linter is where the
guards become enforceable.

2
00:00:02.787 --> 00:00:05.810
Its most important check
is that the two guards sit

3
00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:08.688
at the top of the rule,
ANDed with everything else.

4
00:00:08.688 --> 00:00:11.554
A guard tucked inside an
"or" protects nothing,

5
00:00:11.554 --> 00:00:15.738
yet a simple text search would still
find it and call the rule fine.

6
00:00:15.738 --> 00:00:19.126
That's why the linter works on
the parsed rule, not the text.

7
00:00:19.126 --> 00:00:22.450
Another check is subtler:
"not equal to contractor"

8
00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:25.612
also lets in someone whose
worker type is empty.

9
00:00:25.612 --> 00:00:28.440
The linter flags it,
and the owner decides.
